## 1. Executive summary

Central Finite Curve transitions from a Streamlit RAG prototype (~19 processed DARPG work orders) into a production institutional drafting and governance platform.

Staff will:
1. Search grounded precedent across 50+ institutional files.
2. Generate a Word-compatible draft from QCI templates inside CFC.
3. Edit, chat-refine, and collaborate on that DOCX in SuperDoc.
4. Submit through real QCI line management (PM → SPM → Director/PA).
5. Publish a locked final DOCX into the institutional archive.

### v4 critical upgrades vs v3
1. SuperDoc is the primary document UX (browser + headless).
2. RBAC maps to SuperDoc `role` + `documentMode`.
3. Approval is document-native (comments, tracked changes, locks, clean export).
4. AI chat mutates the open DOCX through Document API / agent tools.
5. Collaboration, version history, and templates are first-class.
6. Object storage + `doc-worker` + collab service are explicit.
7. Document spine is built early (not bolted on after abstract RAG).

