## 3. SuperDoc product scope

### 3.1 Must-have (MVP)
1. Open/edit/export DOCX in CFC (Document Studio).
2. Create draft from template; load/save via authenticated API.
3. Version every meaningful save/submit/decision.
4. Mode/role from RBAC session token.
5. Submit → L1 → L2 → FINAL on the same DOCX.
6. Comments + tracked changes for review.
7. Doc-grounded AI chat that can mutate the open draft (maker) or propose tracked edits (approver).
8. Generate-from-precedent (template + RAG + headless fill → Studio).
9. Export clean final DOCX; retain internal review copy.

### 3.2 Expanded capabilities (phased)
- Template content-controls + field validation gate
- Agent presets: Precedent Weaver, Redline Extender, Completeness Rater, Playbook/style, Clarity, Bulk Updater, Citation Auditor, Value checker, Routing assistant, Finalization packager
- Self-hosted collab presence
- Version diff viewer
- Compare-with-precedent (DOCX diff / PDF text panel)
- Citation bookmarks mapped to chunk IDs
- Deep-link notifications to comment/change anchors
- Admin template library UI
- Knowledge graph navigation into corpus/drafts
- Fixture CI for DOCX round-trips

### 3.3 Explicit non-goals (near term)
- Custom rich-text editor parallel to SuperDoc
- PDF pixel editing as authoring surface
- Liveblocks as default collab
- Auto-FINAL without human L2
- Mobile editing parity
- Replacing QCI email/ERP
- India residency guarantees beyond Railway/vendor posture (revisit if IT mandates)

